      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Doctor: expose systemd linger findings",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add default-disabled structured lint findings for `core/doctor/systemd-linger`\n- keep legacy interactive/non-interactive linger enablement in the existing Doctor run paths\n- gate structured linger findings on the same loaded Gateway systemd service precondition as the legacy Doctor path, so `--all`/`--only` stays quiet on hosts without an OpenClaw systemd user service\n\n## Validation\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run src/flows/doctor-health-contributions.test.ts --reporter=verbose` (72 tests) on rebased head `a39e27b668ee57f4ec3279bb9c6c739af7a3b3a9`\n- `git diff --check`\n- Prior local validation on this slice:\n  - `./node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check src/flows/doctor-health-contributions.ts src/flows/doctor-health-contributions.test.ts`\n  - `./node_modules/.bin/oxlint src/flows/doctor-health-contributions.ts src/flows/doctor-health-contributions.test.ts`\n  - `CI=1 PNPM_CONFIG_VERIFY_DEPS_BEFORE_RUN=false node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs src/flows/doctor-health-contributions.ts src/flows/doctor-health-contributions.test.ts`\n  - `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p tsconfig.core.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core.tsbuildinfo`\n  - `node --max-old-space-size=8192 scripts/plugin-sdk-surface-report.mjs --check`\n  - `node scripts/sync-plugin-sdk-exports.mjs --check`\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior or issue addressed:\nSelected `doctor --lint --only core/doctor/systemd-linger` should not warn merely because local Linux linger is disabled. It should only report disabled linger when OpenClaw is actually running through a loaded Gateway systemd user service, matching the legacy Doctor path.\n\nReal environment tested:\nCrabbox brokered Linux VM, provider `azure`, lease `cbx_6322dfa0e580`, slug `violet-shrimp`, run `run_2dd29a8828cc`, target `linux`, machine type `Standard_D32ads_v6`. The host had real systemd PID 1, an active user systemd manager, `openclaw-gateway.service` enabled as a user unit, and `loginctl show-user crabbox -p Linger` returned `Linger=no`.\n\nExact steps or command run after this patch:\n1. Build source checkout with `pnpm build`.\n2. Create a harmless user unit at `~/.config/systemd/user/openclaw-gateway.service` with `ExecStart=/bin/sleep infinity`.\n3. `systemctl --user daemon-reload`\n4. `systemctl --user enable openclaw-gateway.service`\n5. `systemctl --user is-enabled openclaw-gateway.service`\n6. `loginctl show-user crabbox -p Linger`\n7. `OPENCLAW_SYSTEMD_UNIT=openclaw-gateway OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR=$(mktemp -d) OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH=$(mktemp -d)/config.json ./openclaw.mjs doctor --lint --json --only core/doctor/systemd-linger`\n8. Disable and remove the proof unit, then `systemctl --user daemon-reload`.\n\nEvidence after fix:\n```text\nprovider proof host user=crabbox uid=1000\nsystemd\nLinger=no\n\nsystemctl --user is-enabled openclaw-gateway.service\nenabled\nloginctl show-user crabbox -p Linger\nLinger=no\n\ndoctor_exit=1\n{\"ok\":false,\"checksRun\":1,\"checksSkipped\":32,\"findings\":[{\"checkId\":\"core/doctor/systemd-linger\",\"severity\":\"warning\",\"message\":\"Systemd lingering is disabled for crabbox.\",\"source\":\"doctor\",\"target\":\"systemd.user.crabbox\",\"requirement\":\"systemd user lingering enabled\",\"fixHint\":\"Run: sudo loginctl enable-linger crabbox\"}]}\nASSERT_SYSTEMD_LINGER_FINDING_OK\nPROOF_97514_OK\n```\n\nQuiet-path proof:\nEarlier WSL source CLI proof with `Linger=no` and no loaded Gateway systemd user service exited 0 and emitted no findings:\n```text\n{\"ok\":true,\"checksRun\":1,\"checksSkipped\":32,\"findings\":[]}\n```\n\nObserved result after fix:\nThe selected structured lint check stays quiet when the Gateway service is not loaded, and emits the warning only when a real Linux user systemd service for `openclaw-gateway` is loaded while linger remains disabled. Focused tests on the rebased head cover both the positive selected-lint warning path and the selected quiet path where `readSystemdUserLingerStatus` is not called unless the Gateway service is loaded.\n\nWhat was not tested:\nAfter rebasing to head `a39e27b668ee57f4ec3279bb9c6c739af7a3b3a9`, an exact-head Crabbox rerun was attempted, but the local wrapper timed out and subsequent `crabbox list/history` broker calls returned HTTP 500 (`error code: 1101`). The rebased head passed the focused Doctor contribution test file locally in WSL, and the systemd-linger implementation remains the same loaded-service gate proven by the Crabbox run above.\n\n## Contract\n\nNo config schema, plugin manifest, SDK, persisted data model, or repair-path contract change. This adds only an opt-in structured Doctor lint finding for existing systemd-linger health behavior.\r\n",
